From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:35:48 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cron): a cron result delivered into a chat starts a turn
 there

A cron result for a local chat was always written as a note, so a job an agent created in a chat and delivered back to it sat unread until the user wrote (the agent never saw "the blended-temperature automation did not hold 73" until the user asked "so?").

A job now carries `wake`. A result for a chat of this app starts a turn there when the job's `wake` is true, or when it is unset and the result goes back to the chat the job was created in (deliver `origin`). `wake: false` keeps the note, as does a job delivering to another chat of the app or a script-made job with no origin. A failure notice is always a note. The result is an admission in the chat's FIFO as before, so a running turn finishes first and the result then runs as the next turn; nothing is dropped and one delivery starts one turn.

`wake` is a cronjob_manage argument on create and update, shown in the job's listing, and part of the job definition.
